  "style": {
    "name": "Monochromatic stone harmony",
    "rationale": "A moai is one carved block of volcanic tuff, so the whole mass is gray_concrete with only andesite/stone weather-mottle for tonal break and deepslate reserved for the deep eye-sockets and the brow-shadow band — value, not hue, carves the face. Form follows the document: a single head-and-torso column footed on a buried plinth, head ~45% of the 48-tall height and the dominant volume, with the three recognition motifs projecting in real 3-D — heavy straight brow ridge (~2 forward), long downward-widening wedge nose (~3 forward), and jutting chin/lips. The mass is solid and continuous on all axes (no neck taper), so it reads as a carved monolith from every side of the turntable; the back and far flank mirror the visible half as a deliberate, finished stone surface."
  },
